# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules

# Raycast specific files
raycast-env.d.ts
.raycast-swift-build
.swiftpm
compiled_raycast_swift
compiled_raycast_rust

# misc
.DS_Store
.claude

# NOTE: `.github/` is deliberately NOT ignored — it carries FUNDING.yml and (once
# the standalone mirror exists) CODEOWNERS and sync-from-upstream.yml, matching
# the rest of the fleet. `ray publish` already excludes `.github/` from the Store
# monorepo copy, so ignoring it here would only strip it from the mirror where it
# is actually wanted. (Verified against the published digger/ tree, 2026-07-25.)
# The one exception is `.github/.private/`, ignored below.

# Private notes — .github/.private/ is the standard home for anything that must
# never reach a public repo. It needs BOTH halves below to actually be private:
#
#   1. The `.github/` prefix keeps it out of the RAYCAST STORE monorepo.
#      `ray publish` reads no ignore file — not .gitignore, not
#      .git/info/exclude — and copies the extension root minus one hardcoded
#      list: .git .github .direnv .swiftpm .raycast-swift-build
#      compiled_raycast_rust compiled_raycast_swift node_modules
#      raycast-env.d.ts. `.github` is on that list; a gitignore entry is not a
#      publish exclusion and never was.
#      (Verified in node_modules/@raycast/api/dist/utils/publish/copy-dir.js.)
#
#   2. The ignore entry keeps it out of THIS MIRROR, which is a PUBLIC GitHub
#      repo with the rest of `.github/` tracked in it. Without this line the
#      files would simply leak to a different public place.
#
# Getting only half of this wrong is how a handoff doc carrying seven absolute
# machine paths reached raycast/extensions#30530.
.github/.private/
